.TH SKY 1 "2025-11-23" "QuickSky 1.0.1" "User Commands "
.SH NAME
sky \- lazy developer-friendly native version control tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sky
[\fIOPTION\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
QuickSky is a no-bullshit, standalone version control tool built from scratch to fix the stuff that makes version control feel like a chore. No more memorizing convoluted commands, hopping between directories, or fighting legacy workflows.
.PP
QuickSky is designed for developers who just want to write code, not fight their tools. It provides native, simplified workflows with no dependency on existing tools like Git.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Initialize QuickSky repository in current directory. Prompts for username, remote URL, and main branch name.
.TP
.B upload \fR[\fIMESSAGE\fR]
Commit and push changes to remote repository. If no message provided, auto-generates timestamped commit message.
.TP
.B log
View all commit records in reverse chronological order with SHA, author, timestamp, message, and file changes.
.TP
.B branch \fR[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fINAME\fR]
Branch management operations:
.RS
.TP
.B \-a \fINAME\fR
Create and switch to new branch
.TP
.B \-d \fINAME\fR
Delete branch (cannot delete current branch)
.TP
.B \fINAME\fR
Switch to existing branch
.TP
(no args)
List all branches and show current branch
.RE
.TP
.B change-to \fIREPO-NAME\fR
Switch to different repository by name. QuickSky maintains a global registry of repositories.
.TP
.B rebase \fR[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIRANGE\fR]
Rebase commits with various options:
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-all
Rebase all local changes
.TP
.B \fIYYYY-MM-DD\fR -> \fIYYYY-MM-DD\fR
Rebase commits within date range
.TP
.B fuck-base
Undo last rebase operation
.RE
.TP
.B reload \fICOMMIT-SHA\fR \fINEW-MESSAGE\fR
Edit past commit message by SHA without breaking history.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print help information
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Print version information
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .quicksky/config.toml
Repository configuration file containing user, remote, and branch settings
.TP
.I .quicksky/commits/
Directory containing binary-serialized commit records
.TP
.I .quicksky/branches.json
Branch state tracking file
.TP
.I .quicksky/last_files.json
File hash cache for change detection
.TP
.I ~/.quicksky_registry.json
Global repository registry for repo switching
.TP
.I .skyhide
QuickSky-specific ignore rules (takes precedence over .gitignore)
.TP
.I .gitignore
Standard ignore rules (supported for compatibility)
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Initialize a new repository:
.B sky init
.TP
Upload changes with custom message:
.B sky upload "Fix login bug + add user profile"
.TP
Upload changes with auto-generated message:
.B sky upload
.TP
Create and switch to new branch:
.B sky branch -a feature/payment
.TP
Switch repositories:
.B sky change-to my-other-project
.TP
Rebase all local changes:
.B sky rebase --all
.TP
Rebase commits from date range:
.B sky rebase 2024-10-01 -> 2024-10-05
.TP
Undo last rebase:
.B sky rebase fuck-base
.TP
Edit old commit message:
.B sky reload a1b2c3d "Correct function name (fixes #42)"
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
General error (invalid arguments, file not found, etc.)
